From ee1181d5625f8d8e2bc5aa9b98a2e56368c21008 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:05:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Flagged payments: record management's decision, keep full
 history, review-window wording

- Resolve now records an outcome (refunded / credit given / declined), optional note,
  who decided and when. Declined requires a reason. A decision can't be overwritten.
- Flagged Payments tab: Needs review / Resolved / All with counts, amount, Stripe
  dashboard link, decision details and CSV export. Nothing is ever deleted.
- Amount, currency and payer email are stored when a duplicate is flagged
  (migration b2d4f6a8c0e1, nullable columns only).
- Customer messages and emails no longer promise a refund; they state a 5-business-day review.
- Refund Policy and Terms of Use: duplicate charges are reviewed individually at management's discretion.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
